    "description": "Description This stunning Victorian house is a truly unique and special home, beautifully presented throughout with a perfect balance of warmth, character, and contemporary minimalist design. Offering approximately 1,130 sq ft of internal space, the property has been thoughtfully reconfigured to create a superb modern layout, centred around an impressive open-plan living environment. The sense of light, space, and flow is immediately apparent, making this an exceptional home for both everyday living and entertaining. At the heart of the property is a remarkable 44 ft open-plan kitchen, dining, and reception space, finished to an excellent specification. The contemporary kitchen features a large central island with breakfast bar, quartz worktops, and integrated appliances, forming a natural focal point of the home. This space is complemented by high ceilings, vintage-style radiators, beautiful wood flooring, and timber-framed double-glazed sash windows. Additional benefits include underfloor heating, a Sonos sound system, a feature fireplace, and a striking staircase with glass balustrade. The first floor provides well-balanced accommodation, including a stunning principal bedroom with built-in wardrobes and a modern en-suite bathroom, a generous second double bedroom, a third bedroom/study, and a stylish contemporary shower room. Vaulted ceilings and angled rooflines add further architectural interest and enhance the feeling of space throughout. The outside space has been thoughtfully landscaped to mirror the clean, modern aesthetic of the interior, creating a seamless connection between indoors and out. The rear garden is low-maintenance and beautifully designed, with paved flooring, rendered bench seating with timber detailing, and smart lateral fencing, offering a private and tranquil setting ideal for entertaining. Full-width bifold doors open directly from the main living space, allowing natural light to flood in and enhancing the indoor-outdoor lifestyle this home offers. A truly stunning and individual property, this home combines period charm with high-quality contemporary finishes to create something very special. With its exceptional living space, carefully considered design, and superb presentation throughout, it represents a rare opportunity to acquire a turnkey home that will appeal to discerning buyers seeking both style and substance in equal measure. The location Queens Road is situated in the 'Royals' which is one of East Sheen's most desirable locations, set within a friendly, well-established community that is particularly popular with families and those who enjoy an active, outdoor lifestyle. The surrounding area is rich in green space, with Richmond Park, Palewell Common and the nearby commons all close at hand, offering beautiful settings for walks, cycling and weekend relaxation. The location strikes an ideal balance between tranquillity and convenience. East Sheen's vibrant town centre is just moments away, providing a wide selection of independent shops, cafÃ©s and everyday amenities, while Barnes Village, White Hart Lane and the River Thames are also within easy reach, adding to the area's appeal. Excellent transport links are provided by Mortlake Station, making commuting into central London straightforward. Families are particularly well served, with the highly regarded, ofsted-rated \"Outstanding\" East Sheen Primary School nearby, along with a strong choice of other excellent state and private schools and nurseries. The neighbourhood is known for its welcoming atmosphere, community spirit and active way of life, creating a setting that feels both lively and reassuringly established. Queens Road offers the best of East Sheen living: A central, well-connected location combined with outstanding green spaces, excellent schools and a genuine sense of community - an exceptional place to call home. Council Tax Band: F (London Borough of Richmond upon Thames) Tenure: Freehol",
