    "property_name": "4 bed end terrace house for sale",
    "description": "Ruth Conlon of Keller Williams is delighted to present this beautiful home in an award-winning development, which won the What House Gold Award for Best House 2016. The project ('The Longfords') from Q Developments was created in partnership with 5Plus Architects and was designed to create high-quality, sustainable homes that blend harmoniously with the surrounding neighbourhood. The judges described the homes as 'tardis-like', and praised the well-planned, light-filled living spaces and the seamless flow between them. They highlighted the clever use of timber screens on the front elevations, the striking roof light above the stairs, and the thoughtful colour palette throughout. Nestled within a small, gated mews of three homes, this stunning end-of-terrace contemporary four-bedroom house offers a tranquil retreat with a garden, terraces, off-street parking, and secure entry behind a gatehouse. The gated development, with CCTV, provides peace of mind, making it ideal for frequent travellers or those seeking a secure environment. Entering the home, the light-filled hallway feels spacious and includes a large cloakroom. It leads into an open-plan kitchen/dining/reception room that flows effortlessly into the garden and terrace. The kitchen, designed to be the heart of the home, boasts modern fittings, including two large fridge freezers, two ovens, and a multi-functional tap with instant hot and filtered water. Whether youâre enjoying the breakfast bar or relaxing by the bio-ethanol fireplace, this space is perfect for everyday living. A front section of the room could serve as a cosy reading corner or even accommodate a dining table or piano, as it once did for the current owner. Downstairs, the oak staircase leads to a versatile family room or guest suite with fitted wardrobes, opening onto a second terrace connected to the main garden. This space offers endless possibilities-ideal as an office, playroom, games room, or hobby room. The lower level also features a full-sized bathroom, utility room, and generous pantry or storage room. It could even function as independent living quarters, with its own separate side access for added convenience.The space is constructed with waterproof caltite reinforced concrete and includes a secondary cavity drainage system for added durability. On the top floor, the master suite offers a peaceful retreat with a view of the garden, with a small terrace, fitted wardrobes, and an en-suite shower room. A family bathroom, second bedroom, and third single bedroom, currently used as an office, complete this level. The home is equipped with modern technology, including recessed downlights with dimmer switches, sky+ cabling, TV and radio antennae, underfloor heating, and a ventilating heat recovery system. The development also features eco-friendly materials, with slate roofs, green roofs, and masonry elevations incorporating wet-cast stone assemblies. The annual service charge for the mews is approximately Â£850. EPC rating C. The location is perfect for those seeking access to both central London and the airport, with Teddington and Hampton Wick stations nearby. Whether commuting to Heathrow, Waterloo, or King's Cross, you can be there within an hour and now within the 'super-loop express' Heathrow and parts of London are more accessible than they have ever been, via Teddington. For those who enjoy nature, the historical Hampton Court and Bushy Park are just moments away, while Kingston offers excellent shopping options, including the Fenwick Centre. The exclusive Lensbury Club is also nearby, and the area is served by top-rated schools, including Collis, Hampton Wick &amp; St John The Baptist, and secondary schools like Teddington, Grey Court, and Turing House. Teddington High Street is the heart of this charming, riverside town, offering a perfect blend of traditional village appeal and modern convenience. Lined with a variety of independent boutiques, trendy cafes, and high-end restaurants, itâs the perfect place to spend a leisurely afternoon or enjoy a night out. Whether youâre looking for unique homeware, artisanal food, or a refreshing drink in one of the cozy pubs, the High Street caters to all tastes. With its picturesque surroundings, friendly atmosphere, and easy access to the River Thames, Teddington High Street is a vibrant and welcoming hub for both locals and visitors alike. Also just a short walk away is Hampton Wick. A quaint area also offering a selection of independent shops, cafes and traditional pubs, as well as excellent transport links. A quick short cut under Kingston bridge and you are on the banks of the River Thames, offering the perfect setting for a leisurely stroll with your dog or a scenic run along the water. What does the current owner love? Owning this modern home has allowed for a lifestyle of luxury, comfort, and style, with every detail thoughtfully designed. The prime location adds an extra layer of convenience, while the added security ensures peace of mind. What do I love? I was immediately impressed by the tall ceilings and the grand front door, which set the tone for a home that feels both expansive and welcoming. I love the shops and restaurants in Teddington high street, and a family favourite pub is also The Anglers on the riverside. Viewings are highly recommended. Get in touch to book",
