    "property_name": "3 bed detached house for sale",
    "description": "A detached three bedroom family home located on a popular residential road, close to Marney's Village Inn, duck pond and Esher common. This traditional family home retains architectural features of the art-deco period together with updated 'charcoal grey' double glazed windows fitted to a Crittall style across the front elevation to preserve its original style and appearance. The property is arranged naturally over two floors, is extended at ground floor level and benefits from a beautifully established rear garden of abt. 80ft, a lawned front garden with off-street-parking and a side driveway leading to a detached garage. The accommodation is already well balanced but there is plenty of scope to extend, adapt or re-model if desired. This comfortable family home is well presented throughout and consists of an attractive recessed storm porch with panelled front door completed with stained and leaded glazing with matching side windows. This leads to a good size entrance hall with under stair coats cupboard and useful guest W.C. There are two very nice interconnecting reception rooms with ornamental fireplaces, leading through to an extended kitchen / diner with natural wood flooring, which looks over and provides access to the garden via double doors. To complete the ground floor there is an excellent utility area with superb storage solutions, and an external door opening to side access. Upstairs, you will find a return staircase with half-landing window, three double bedrooms; the principle and second bedrooms both feature bay windows and built-in wardrobes, whilst the third bedroom features a pretty corner window. All bedrooms are supported by a good size main family bathroom fitted with a modern suite, complete with double ended bath and separate shower. Externally, the gardens are established with a variety of plants, trees and shrubs with lawns front and rear, and both sunny and shaded areas in the back garden to enjoy the natural sun light. There is a separate tool shed behind the garage. Location: Elm Tree Avenue is a sought after residential road within close proximity of mainline stations (Esher, 0.8 miles) and (Thames Ditton, 0.6 miles) providing direct trains to London Waterloo in around 23 and 31 minutes respectively. By road, the A3 is under 2 miles away, providing access to central London, the M25 and the motorway network. Esher High Street is only 1.4 miles away, there you will find an Everyman cinema, several coffee shops, a Waitrose supermarket, as well as a great range of restaurants and bars. The local shops and amenities of both Thames Ditton village (1.4 miles) and Hampton Court Village (1.6 miles) are also accessible. More extensive shopping is found in nearby Kingston upon Thames (3.3 miles). The world famous Hampton Court Palace and grounds plays host to annual cultural events, concerts and an outdoor cinema, with royal parks (Bushy &amp; Home) for extensive outdoor activities, including beautiful riverside walks along the banks the River Thames. The Elmbridge area is popular with families and offers an excellent choice of state and independent schools",
