    "description": "Beautiful Victorian home in sought-after location Description Dating back to the 1890s this charming Victorian home, located in the ever-popular Manor Road within the Kent Town Conservation Area, retains many of its original period features and offers light-filled and well-presented accommodation. A welcoming entrance hall leads to the front reception room, a wonderful space boasting a large bay window and stunning feature fireplace. This room flows seamlessly into the adjacent rear sitting room, which enjoys two built in dressers and a sash window providing additional natural light. Further to the rear, the well-appointed kitchen provides excellent storage and work top space, as well as delightful views of the garden. It opens into a large dining area with a vaulted ceiling and Velux window, flooding the space with natural light. From here double doors lead to the garden, while an additional door opens onto a courtyard area with access to two useful storage rooms. A shower room with toilet completes the ground floor accommodation. Upstairs, the principal bedroom is situated to the front of the property and enjoys three sash windows and two sets of built-in wardrobes. Bedrooms two and three are comfortable doubles, positioned either side of the family bathroom. Above, an impressive loft room offers excellent storage and exciting potential for conversion into additional bedroom accommodation if required (subject to the necessary consents). Externally to the rear, there is a mature garden which is mainly laid to lawn with a smart terrace providing space for al fresco dining and entertaining. Mature beds frame the lawn showcasing a colourful array of shrubs and blooms. To the front of the property the driveway provides off-street parking. Please note the photos shown were taken in July 2024. Location Manor Road is a highly popular residential road positioned just 0.5 miles from Bridge Road (also known locally as Hampton Court Village) with its superb range of independent shops, boutiques, bars and restaurants. More extensive shopping is accessible in Kingston upon Thames. Riverside walks along the Thames towpath are also only 0.5 miles from the property, as is East Molesey Cricket Club and Molesey Boat Club, which both offer clubs and facilities for children and adults. Transport links in the area are excellent with a regular and direct rail service to London Waterloo from Hampton Court Station (0.6 miles) in only 35 minutes. The M4, M3 and M25 motorways are within easy driving distance and central London itself is approximately 12.5 miles away. The property is well situated for an excellent selection of both state and independent schools, including nearby St. Lawrence and The Orchard schools which are both 0.2 miles from the property. Square Footage: 1,704 sq f",
