    "property_name": "4 bed town house for sale",
    "description": "Tudors are pleased to offer for sale this four bedroom terraced town house which is located in a desirable cul-de-sac within the Hurst Park development. Offered to the market with no onward chain, the property has been within the same family since 1970, circa 55 years. The Hurst Park development is well regarded and offers lots of park land recreational fields to enjoy afternoon strolls with the River Thames with towpath beside leading up to Hampton Court with its Palace, restaurants, boutiques, cafes and train station â ideal for the commuter, Oyster zone 6 and also Bushy Park â With over 1000 acres. The property also enjoys being close to primary schools, local supermarkets and East Molesey village with its shops/restaurants/bars and cafes. Bus routes connect Hampton Court, Kingston (with comprehensive shopping), Walton on Thames and Hersham village. Nearby there are many sporting facilities in the area including; East Molesey cricket club, Molesey Rowing club, Molesey sailing club, Molesey football club, Hurst swimming Pool and the Pavilion sports club with swimming pool and Tennis Courts. The property comprises: An entrance hallway with access to an 18ft integral garage, a downstairs cloakroom, a utility room with door leading to the garden and a downstairs bedroom four/study with French doors opening onto a westerly facing garden. Stairs from the hallway lead up to a bright and spacious 17ft x 16ft living room with front aspect windows, a dining room which leads onto a kitchen. The kitchen has many eye/base level units/cupboards with worktop area. Further stairs lead up to a landing with access to two double bedrooms, a single bedroom (all bedrooms with built in wardrobes), and a bathroom with white suite. Externally there is a walled rear garden which is westerly facing with patio and artificial grass area along with mature shrub borders and rear access gate. To the front there is a driveway providing off road parking which leads to the integral garage with up/over door with power/light. Other benefits include: UPVC Double-glazing. (EPC Rating = D) Elmbridge borough Council = E",
