    "property_name": "3 bed terraced house for sale",
    "description": "Three bedroom home in wonderful riverside location with garage. Description With a superb location in the tranquil Thames Meadow enclave of West Molesey, this three-bedroom home offers an exceptional opportunity for first-time buyers or renovators seeking a project with immense potential. With Hurst Park and the River Thames just a few steps from the rear garden gate, the location is as idyllic as it is convenient. The ground floor welcomes you through a practical porch with access to a guest WC and coat cupboard. Beyond, a spacious reception room features a unique floor-to-ceiling front aspect window and a characterful fireplace, creating a bright and inviting living space. The open-plan layout flows seamlessly into the rear aspect dining room, where sliding doors bathe the area in natural light and open directly onto the garden. Folding wooden shutters separate the dining room from the kitchen, which enjoys a rear outlook and is fitted with a range of base and wall units. A secondary door leads to a generous storage area housing the boiler. Upstairs, the first floor comprises three bedrooms-all with fitted wardrobes-and a family bathroom. Bedroom two is particularly special, offering picturesque views over Hurst Park and the River Thames. Externally, the rear garden features a mix of terrace and lawn, bordered by planting beds and enhanced by direct access to the park and riverside. The front garden is laid to lawn, and the property comes with a garage. Location Thames Meadow is a delightful road located within half a mile of local amenities such as a Tesco supermarket, leisure pool and playground and is perfectly placed for walks along the River Thames. The Bridge Road area of East Molesey (also known locally as Hampton Court Village) is around a mile away and has a range of independent shops, boutiques, bars and restaurants. The River Thames, Hampton Court Palace, Bushy Park and Hurst Park are all within easy reach. Hampton Court station is also less than a mile away from the property and provides regular and direct trains to London Waterloo (from 33 minutes). The house uniquely backs onto 'Hurst Meadows'; a beautiful park ideal for dog walkers, runners or even a spot of boules! Also nearby are East Molesey Cricket Club and Molesey Boat Club which are both highly regarded in the local community. The Elmbridge Borough is popular with families as it has an impressive array of both independent and state schools. Square Footage: 991 sq f",
