    "description": "Contemporary home with wonderful garden in sought-after location. Description This property has a wonderfully individual character, shaped by its origins and long family ownership. Built in 1969 by Mr Biss, a well known local architect, it carries the hallmarks of thoughtful mid century design: Generous proportions, an eclectic layout and beautiful wooden doors imported from Asia that give the interior a warm, crafted feel. Having remained in the same family for over fifty years, it comes to the market with no onwards chain. The galleried hallway provides an impressive, light-filled entrance. To the right is a generous dining room with large front aspect window and an open connection to the reception room behind. To the other side of the entrance hall is the kitchen, which offers plenty of built in storage and a number of integrated appliances. The lower ground floor provides a practical and versatile foundation to the home. A spacious laundry room sits alongside a study, both of which could easily be used as a cosy cinema, gaming space or gym if required. The principal reception room can be found on the raised ground floor. Stretching generously across the rear of the property, this room creates an inviting setting for family life and entertaining, with sliding doors opening onto the rear garden. A connecting door from the reception room leads through to an adjoining store room which is unusually large and adaptable. The garage, accessed via stairs from the store, houses the boiler and provides external access to the garden via a rear door. The upper floors offer a well balanced arrangement of bedrooms. The rear aspect principal bedroom includes fitted wardrobes and an ensuite bathroom with bath and separate shower. There are three further bedrooms, one with a wall of fitted wardrobes, in addition to the family bathroom with the convenience of twin sinks. Outside, the garden is a standout feature-mature, private, and beautifully established. A covered outdoor kitchen area makes it perfect for relaxed gatherings and summer entertaining. The property also benefits from planning permission (ref: 2017/1799) for a first floor side extension and an additional front rooflight, offering clear potential for future expansion while respecting the homeâs original design. Please note the property has been virtually staged to show how some of the rooms can be utilised. Location Hansler Grove is a sought after residential road in the heart of East Molesey, conveniently located for the amenities of Walton Road and Bridge Road, both providing a mix of restaurants, coffee shops and boutiques. Kingston-upon-Thames is nearby (2.4 miles) and provides a wider selection of shopping. Hampton Court Station is just half a mile away and provides regular and direct trains into London Waterloo in around 33 minutes. Hampton Court Palace (0.7 miles) and Bushy Park (1 mile) are also easily accessible for days out and there is an excellent choice of both state and independent schools in the area, making it ideal for families. The M25 (10 miles) provides access to both Heathrow and Gatwick airports. Please note all distances and times are approximate. Square Footage: 2,673 sq f",
