    "property_name": "4 bed terraced house for sale",
    "description": "\"In a market where truly characterful family homes in prime Teddington locations are increasingly difficult to secure, Blackmores Grove represents a compelling opportunity to acquire a substantial period property. .\" Ryan - Branch Manager, Devenports. A beautifully proportioned period family home, perfectly positioned on one of Teddington's most sought-after residential roads, Blackmores Grove effortlessly combines character, space and practicality in a location that continues to be highly prized by families and professionals alike. Internally, the accommodation extends to approximately 1,650 sq ft and has been thoughtfully arranged to suit modern family life. The ground floor offers a series of bright and versatile reception spaces, ideal for both relaxed family living and entertaining, whilst retaining much of the character and warmth associated with homes of this era. Large windows allow natural light to flood through the property, creating a welcoming atmosphere throughout. The kitchen and dining areas form the heart of the home, providing an inviting space for family gatherings, informal meals and social occasions alike. Upstairs, four well-proportioned bedrooms and two bathrooms provide comfortable accommodation for growing families, with a layout that offers flexibility for home working, guest accommodation or children's rooms as needs evolve over time. One of the property's standout qualities is its sense of balance. It is large enough to accommodate modern family demands whilst retaining a comfortable, manageable feel that many larger homes can lack. The rear garden is another notable feature, offering a wonderfully private and low-maintenance outdoor space. Thoughtfully landscaped and framed by mature planting, it provides an attractive extension of the living accommodation, while the contemporary bi-fold doors create a seamless connection between the house and garden. Whether hosting friends on a summer evening, enjoying family time outdoors, or simply relaxing with a coffee in the morning sun, the garden strikes an excellent balance between usability, privacy and visual appeal. Location is, of course, a significant part of the appeal. Blackmores Grove enjoys a reputation as one of Teddington's most desirable roads, combining a peaceful residential setting with exceptional convenience. Teddington High Street, with its independent cafÃ©s, restaurants, boutiques and everyday amenities, is within easy reach, while excellent transport links provide straightforward access into central London. The area is also renowned for its outstanding schools, abundance of green space and proximity to the River Thames, all of which contribute to its enduring popularity. Perhaps most importantly, this is a house with genuine longevity. It offers the kind of space, location and character that buyers often spend years searching for, together with the opportunity to enjoy and, over time, further enhance a home that already provides an exceptional foundation for family life",
