    "property_name": "3 bed semi-detached house for sale",
    "description": "Presenting this well-proportioned three bedroom end terrace house, ideally situated on a private road and offering excellent access to local shops and amenities. The property features a spacious and welcoming entrance hall, leading to a bright and airy living room that flows seamlessly into a modern fitted kitchen with ample storage and worktop space. Upstairs, three generously sized bedrooms provide comfortable family accommodation, complemented by a contemporary family bathroom. The house benefits from a driveway providing off-street parking for multiple vehicles. Immaculately maintained throughout, this home offers scope to extend (subject to planning permission), allowing buyers the opportunity to further enhance the living space to suit their needs. The propertyâs layout is both practical and versatile, appealing to families and professionals alike. With its sought-after location, well-presented interiors and potential for future development, this attractive home represents an excellent opportunity for those seeking a move-in ready property with room to grow. Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this delightful house has to offer. Location Discover Epsom â A Desirable Surrey Town Epsom is a historic and highly sought-after market town in Surrey, offering an ideal balance of countryside charm and modern convenience. Just 15 miles from London, itâs a top choice for families and professionals who want green space without compromising on connectivity. Epsom station provides direct trains to London Waterloo, Victoria, and London Bridge in under 40 minutes, while major roads like the A3 and M25 are easily accessible. The town is best known for the world-famous Epsom Derby and is surrounded by beautiful open spaces including Epsom Downs, Horton Country Park, and Nonsuch Park. These green areas are perfect for walking, cycling, and enjoying the outdoors. Epsomâs vibrant town centre offers a variety of shops, cafÃ©s, pubs, and restaurants, plus the Ashley Centre for retail and the Epsom Playhouse for entertainment. Weekly markets and local events add to its strong community feel. Families are especially drawn to Epsom for its excellent schools, such as Rosebery, Glyn, and the prestigious Epsom College. Housing in the area ranges from charming period homes and Edwardian villas to modern apartments and family houses, with popular areas including Woodcote, College Area, and nearby Ewell Village. With its mix of heritage, greenery, excellent amenities, and great schools, Epsom continues to be one of Surreyâs most desirable places to live. Disclaimer Kaybridge Residential is a trading name of kbr Group Ltd. Registered in England &amp; Wales, Company No: 16532664. Registered Office: 23 Stoneleigh Broadway, Epsom, KT17 2JE. Every care has been taken in the preparation of property particulars, but we do not guarantee the accuracy of the information provided. The details are intended as a general guide and do not constitute, nor form part of, an offer or contract. All measurements, floor areas, distances, and descriptions are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact. Prospective purchasers/tenants must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each statement contained in these particulars. Fixtures, fittings, and appliances referred to have not been tested, and no guarantee can be given that they are in working order. Kaybridge Residential, its employees, or representatives have no authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatsoever in relation to a property",
